    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "b\nn\ne\nS\nS\nwine list\nc la\nS •",
      "WINE LIST\nCHAMPAGNE\nBRUT\nBILLECART-SALMON\nRED WINES\nMERCUREY\nBillecart-Salmon Brut Champagne\nThe house of Billecart-Salmon was founded in\n1818 in Marevil Sur Ay near Epernay, in the\nheart of the Champagne region. This cuvée\nis a blend of 35% Chardonnay, 35% Pinot\nNoir and 30% Pinot Meunier grapes which\ncome from the very best vineyards in Marne.\nIts bright straw-colour is complemented by a\nsteady mousse of slowly rising bubbles. Its\nnose is of ripe pears with a delicate touch of\ncut hay. Billecart-Salmon has an elegant\nfruity flavour, leaving a clean fresh taste in\nMercurey Domaine Louis Max 2001\nMercurey Domaine Louis Max 2001 was\nproduced in the Burgundy - Côte\nChalonnaise area using 100% Pinot Noir\ngrapes. It is deep and intense cherry red in\ncolour. Its bouquet is powerful, with\nconcentrated aromas of raspberry,\nblackberry, liquorice and vanilla. This wine\noffers a pleasant taste of wood and a good\nbalance between fine tannins and fruit.\nEnjoy this wine with red meat, game or ripe\ncheeses.\nPOUILLY- FUISSE\nstum Lendan\nJaboulet-Vercherre Pouilly Fuissé 2002\nThe Pouilly Fuissé vineyards are located at\nMâconnais, the southern part of Burgundy,\nFrance. Jaboulet-Vercherre Pouilly Fuissé\n2002 is produced from 100% Chardonnay\ngrapes. Pale gold in colour, the 2002\nvintage is fresh, rich in fruit characters with\nhoney notes and a long aftertaste. It goes\nwell with seafood dishes particularly those in\na cream sauce.\nGREEN\nPOINT\nVieux Château Landon, Cru Bourgeois\nVieux Château Landon is a small Château\nsituated in Médoc which has a very limited\nproduction every year. The 2001 vintage is\ndeep ruby in colour, with delicate dark\ncherry and matured red fruit characters,\nand a touch of chocolate and prune\nflavours. It is full bodied with soft tannins.\nThis delicious wine goes very well with\nmost of the meat dishes.\nGreen Point Yarra Valley Chardonnay 2004\nThe 2004 Green Point Yarra Valley\nChardonnay is a pale straw colour with a\ngreen hue. The wine has complex characters\nthat includes hints of fresh peaches,\ncinnamon and spicy vanillin oak. The use of\nfine French oak barriques adds structure and\nlength to the back palate, and the finish is\nlong, lingering and crisp.\nCX SIGNATURE DRINKS\nPORT\nDOWS\nLATE SO PORTANTAGE\n1999\nDow's Late Bottled Vintage Port 1999\nThis wine is sourced from the same vineyards\nthat in exceptional years produce Dow's\nrenowned Vintage Ports. It is aged solely in oak\ncasks and bottled 5 to 6 years after the harvest.\nIt is a full rich Port with spicy fruit flavours and\nan elegant aromatic nose, well rounded on the\npalate and has the traditional Dow's drier\nfinish. This makes it one of the finest Late\nBottled Vintage Ports available.\nAPERITIES AND COCKTAILS\nGin • Rum • Vodka • Martini Rosso • Martini\nExtra Dry • Campari • Sweet and Dry Sherry •\nBloody Mary • Screwdriver\nWHISKIES\nChivas Regal 12 Years Old\nJohnnie Walker Gold Label\nJack Daniel's Bourbon\nCanadian Club\nCOGNAC\nHine 'Rare and Delicate' Fine Champagne\nLIQUEURS\nDrambuie • Contreau • Bailey's Irish Cream\nBEER\nInternational Selection\nCATHAY DELIGHT\nA kiwifruit based non-alcoholic\ndrink with coconut juice and a\ntouch of fresh mint.\nPACIFIC SUNRISE\nA refreshing combination of\nchampagne and Drambuie with\nthe zest of orange and lemon.\nCathay Pacific aims to offer a diverse selection of wines on\nboard - but apologies if on some flights a certain wine is\nnot available. Our crew will always be happy to\nrecommend an alternative.\nCX702, 706, 708, 712, 754(BKK/HKG)\n1-6-2005",
      "menu\nbusi\nbusine\nclas"
    ],
